//
//  ItundaFaceSymbols.swift
//  itundaface Symbols -- iOS port of the same phase-8 batch shipped to
//  bank-mfe/Android same session. Real Noto Emoji silhouette data (github.com/
//  googlefonts/noto-emoji, SIL Open Font License 1.1, see
//  /NOTICE_THIRD_PARTY.md at the repo root), same real-sourcing approach as
//  phases 2-7. 8 real glyphs (Check Mark Button, Cross Mark, Exclamation
//  Mark, Question Mark, Hundred, Prohibited, Recycling, Warning), extending
//  itundaface's emoji-input registry to 68 glyphs across 8 categories.
//
//  Real gradient found and resolved (Warning's "!" mark): a genuine 2-stop
//  linear gradient (#424242 -> #212121, not degenerate -- the 2 stops
//  genuinely differ) resolved to the real start stop (#424242) as the flat
//  substitute, matching every prior phase's "read the actual stops, don't
//  invent a color" discipline. A separate real opacity:0.2 duplicate of the
//  same "!" shape (a soft drop-shadow) was dropped as pure decoration, same
//  judgment call every phase makes for shading vs. semantic content.
//
//  Real polygon->path conversion (Prohibited's diagonal slash-bar accent):
//  no polygon primitive exists in this glyph vocabulary, and a closed
//  straight-edged polygon converts losslessly to a path with only M/L/Z
//  commands -- no new primitive needed for this one real, simple case.
//
//  REQUIRED ATTRIBUTION: see /NOTICE_THIRD_PARTY.md at the repo root (OFL
//  clause 2 requires the license notice travel with any copy).
//

